concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-3-sec-2-ss-1b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2(1B) Subsection 15HK(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-2-ss-1b ;
    values:originalText "(1B) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and  (b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of the person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person; and  (c) the person discloses the information; and  (d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and  (e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:  (i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of any person or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled operation;  (ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any person or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled operation.  Controlled operation disclosure offence  Schedule 3  No. 75, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other Measures) Act 2018  Note: Recklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1B)(b) and (d) and subparagraph (1B)(e)(ii)—see section 5.6 of the Criminal Code. Penalty: Imprisonment for 10 years." ;
